msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:83
msgid "`nix-env` parses the symbolic derivation name `firefox.*` as:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:87
msgid "\"firefox.*\""
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:88
msgid "\"\""
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:92
msgid ""
"The `name` parts of the _arguments_ to `nix-env` are treated as extended "
"regular expressions and matched against the `name` parts of derivation names "
"in the package source. The match is case-sensitive. The regular expression "
"can optionally be followed by a dash (`-`) and a version number; if omitted, "
"any version of the package will match. For details on regular expressions, "
"see [**regex**(7)](https://linux.die.net/man/7/regex)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:99
msgid "Common patterns for finding package names with `nix-env`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:101
msgid "`firefox`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:103
msgid "Matches the package name `firefox` and any version."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:105
msgid "`firefox-32.0`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:107
msgid "Matches the package name `firefox` and version `32.0`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:109
msgid "`gtk\\\\+`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:111
msgid ""
"Matches the package name `gtk+`. The `+` character must be escaped using a "
"backslash (`\\`) to prevent it from being interpreted as a quantifier, and "
"the backslash must be escaped in turn with another backslash to ensure that "
"the shell passes it on."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:114
msgid "`.\\*`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:116
msgid "Matches any package name. This is the default for most commands."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:119
msgid "`'.*zip.*'`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:121
msgid ""
"Matches any package name containing the string `zip`. Note the dots: "
"`'*zip*'` does not work, because in a regular expression, the character `*` "
"is interpreted as a quantifier."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:124
msgid "`'.*(firefox|chromium).*'`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:126
msgid ""
"Matches any package name containing the strings `firefox` or `chromium`."
msgstr ""

