#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:139
msgid "It is loaded as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:141
msgid "If the default expression is a file, it is loaded as a Nix expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:142
msgid ""
"If the default expression is a directory containing a `default.nix` file, "
"that `default.nix` file is loaded as a Nix expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:143
msgid ""
"If the default expression is a directory without a `default.nix` file, then "
"its contents (both files and subdirectories) are loaded as Nix expressions. "
"The expressions are combined into a single attribute set, each expression "
"under an attribute with the same name as the original file or subdirectory. "
"Subdirectories without a `default.nix` file are traversed recursively in "
"search of more Nix expressions, but the names of these intermediate "
"directories are not added to the attribute paths of the default Nix "
"expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:147
msgid "Then, the resulting expression is interpreted like this:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:149
msgid ""
"If the expression is an attribute set, it is used as the default Nix "
"expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:150
msgid ""
"If the expression is a function, an empty set is passed as argument and the "
"return value is used as the default Nix expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env.md:154
msgid ""
"If the default expression contains two files, `foo.nix` and `bar.nix`, then "
"the default Nix expression will be equivalent to"
msgstr ""

